6.To make an image act as a link, where should the <img> tag be placed?
A)Inside the <a> tag //answers
B)Before the <a> tag
C)After the <a> tag
D)Inside the href attribute


✅ Correct Answer: A. Inside the <a> tag

Explanation (Simple)

To make an image clickable, place the <img> tag inside the <a> (anchor) tag.

Example:
<a href="https://example.com">
  <img src="logo.png" alt="Logo">
</a>

When the user clicks the image, they are taken to the link specified in the href attribute.

Why not the others?
✅ A. Inside the <a> tag → Correct.
❌ B. Before the <a> tag → The image won't be part of the link.
❌ C. After the <a> tag → The image won't be clickable.
❌ D. Inside the href attribute → Invalid HTML.

✅ Correct Answer: A. Inside the <a> tag


7.What is the purpose of the hreflang attribute?
A)To set the link color
B)To specify the language of the linked document  //answer
C)To set the page title
D)To link to a script 

✅ Correct Answer: B. To specify the language of the linked document

Explanation (Simple)

The hreflang attribute tells browsers and search engines the language (and optionally the region) of the linked page.

Example:

<a href="https://example.com/en" hreflang="en">English</a>

<a href="https://example.com/fr" hreflang="fr">French</a>

Here:

hreflang="en" → English page
hreflang="fr" → French page
Why not the others?
❌ A. To set the link color → Use CSS.
✅ B. To specify the language of the linked document → Correct.
❌ C. To set the page title → Use the title attribute or the <title> tag.
❌ D. To link to a script → Use the <script> tag.

✅ Correct Answer: B. To specify the language of the linked document


8.Which character is used to separate the email address from the query parameters in a mailto link?
A)&
B);
C)? //answer
D)#

✅ Correct Answer: C. ?

Explanation (Simple)

In a mailto: link, the ? character separates the email address from the query parameters (such as subject, body, cc, etc.).

Example:
<a href="mailto:abc@example.com?subject=Hello&body=How are you?">
  Send Email
</a>

Here:

mailto:abc@example.com → Email address
? → Starts the query parameters
subject=Hello → Email subject
&body=How are you? → Additional parameter
Why not the others?
❌ A. & → Separates multiple query parameters.
❌ B. ; → Not used for separating query parameters in a mailto: URL.
✅ C. ? → Correct! Separates the email address from the query parameters.
❌ D. # → Used for page fragments (anchors), not mailto: parameters.

✅ Correct Answer: C. ?


9.Can a mailto: link include a "CC" address?
A)No
B)Yes, using ?cc=address@email.com  //answer
C)Only in Outlook
D)Only with JavaScript


✅ Correct Answer: B. Yes, using ?cc=address@email.com

Explanation (Simple)

A mailto: link can include a CC (Carbon Copy) email address by using the cc query parameter.

Example:
<a href="mailto:john@example.com?cc:jane@example.com">
  Send Email
</a>

Correct syntax (with =):

<a href="mailto:john@example.com?cc=jane@example.com">
  Send Email
</a>

You can also include multiple parameters:

<a href="mailto:john@example.com?cc=jane@example.com&subject=Meeting&body=Hello">
  Send Email
</a>
Why not the others?
❌ A. No → Incorrect. mailto: supports cc.
✅ B. Yes, using ?cc=address@email.com → Correct.
❌ C. Only in Outlook → Incorrect. It's supported by many email clients.
❌ D. Only with JavaScript → Incorrect. JavaScript is not required.

✅ Correct Answer: B. Yes, using ?cc=address@email.com


10.Which prefix is used in the href attribute to initiate a phone call on mobile devices?
A)call:
B)phone:
C)tel:
D)dial:


✅ Correct Answer: C. tel:

Explanation (Simple)

The tel: prefix is used in the href attribute to create a clickable phone number. On mobile devices, tapping the link opens the phone dialer.

Example:
<a href="tel:+919876543210">Call Us</a>

When the user clicks "Call Us", the phone app opens with the number ready to dial.

Why not the others?
❌ A. call: → Not a valid URI scheme.
❌ B. phone: → Not a valid URI scheme.
✅ C. tel: → Correct! Used for phone numbers.
❌ D. dial: → Not a valid URI scheme.

✅ Correct Answer: C. tel: